+# TLS backend
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use Rustls as the TLS backend, chosen because it fits the Rust codebase, has had fewer CVEs, and is simpler. Later recorded decisions on TLS (HTTPS everywhere with no plaintext exception, and self-signed certificates for testing) concern where and how TLS is used, not which backend provides it, so they do not change this choice.
